   "note": "The wormhole mechanism here is purely compile-time \u2014 a 64-slot lookup table, no traversal, no neighborhood coupling, no threshold or cascade in any local update rule \u2014 so the 8/8 versus 0/20 split carries zero certified randomness or interference provenance and no Bell witness. Cost-wise, that table is fixed overhead paid once at compile time rather than per-step spend, but the record reports no token budget or speed figure, so the economics of the 28-run comparison remain an honest null.",
